The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) calls every report one issue. The reports show three
problems. Each one has its own ticket now.

<Callout>
Three problems, three fixes. The queued parser fix closes only the first one.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

- **parser.** The shared parser reads every date month first. Day first tenants see day and
  month flip. "7 April went out on 4 July."
- **hint.** The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type the month
  first, as told. The form reads the day first. Only form reports from booking-v3 tenants.
- **move.** The date moves by one day, not a flip. "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in
  Toronto got Monday." This looks like a time zone bug. The desk listed these reports in
  `desk-notes.json`.

## How we counted

1. The export repeats some reports, because its pages overlap. We count each report id once.
2. We place a report by its tenant and the way it came in (`causes.ts`), not by its intake tag.
   Intake guesses the tag from the browser language, so many tags point to the wrong problem.
3. A report the desk read as a one-day move counts under `move`.

## Why it was one ticket

Triage merges reports by subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
All three problems arrive with the same few subject lines, and triage never reads the body.
So they landed in one ticket.

